			"notes": "First release of Paxi Extra, a continuation of [Paxi Plus](https://modrinth.com/mod/paxiplus) by Lancet_, now on NeoForge and Fabric for 1.21.1 and 26.1 through 26.1.2.\n\n- Built-in resource packs and data packs added by mods can go in your load order. Write the pack's ID instead of a file name, and it loads exactly where you put it. `fabric` and `mod_resources` work too, if you want all the mod assets at a particular spot in the stack.\n- Packs sitting in `config/paxi/resourcepacks` and `datapacks` are no longer force-loaded unless the load order names them, so a pack can be left in the folder without being active.\n- The datapack folder and its load order file are created at start-up rather than the first time a world loads, so a fresh instance has both to edit right away.\n- A `--user--` flag decides where your own packs sit. Anything above it goes under the packs you picked yourself, anything below stays on top.\n\nGrab the file matching your loader; the jar name ends in `-neoforge` or `-fabric`."
		}
